            <ArticleTitle>Graphical computer techniques for improving the detection of myocardiac ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>335-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Traditional investigative methods to detect and localise cardiac abnormalities are often difficult and time consuming. The use of minicomputers has made a dramatic impact on non-invasive diagnostic techniques in cardiac patients. The Cardiology Division of the Geneva University Hospital has assembled a minicomputer-based data acquisition/visualisation system to study cardiac structures and their associated motions using radionuclide techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
